---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="LGBTQ+ Tulum Tours | Queerness Experiences" description={"LGBTQ+ Tulum tours for queer and trans travelers and families: secret cenote, Muyil river float, jungle and monkeys, food tour, and Town Chisme."}>

<header class="head">
  <div class="head-top">
    <div class="shape-y"></div>
    <p class="head-eye">★ Small-group tours</p>
    <h1>LGBTQ+ Tulum Tours</h1>
    <p>Curated for sapphic, queer, and trans people. Every tour is small and personal, often just your group. Tap any tour to see what the day looks like.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="food-feature" style="position:relative;z-index:2;margin-top:var(--s-md);margin-bottom:0;">
    <p class="food-feature-caption">Eating deliciously is a priority. Local bakeries, locally-owned restaurants, an amazing chef, seasonal local fruit. Every tour is tailored to dietary restrictions and allergies.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="tours">
  <div style="max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto var(--s-md);padding:0 var(--s-sm);">
    <p style="background:var(--bone);border:3px solid var(--dark);box-shadow:6px 6px 0 var(--magenta);padding:18px 22px;font-size:17px;font-weight:500;color:var(--dark);line-height:1.6;">On these tours, we'll talk cultural nuances, Mexican ingenuity, and queer activism in Latin America.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="tour-grid">

  <!-- SECRET CENOTE -->
  <div class="tour">
    <input type="checkbox" id="tour1" checked>
    <label class="tour-head" for="tour1">
      <img class="tour-photo" src="/images/secret-cenote-cave.jpg" alt="Entering the Secret Cenote through the cave in Tulum">
      <div class="tour-tag">For the adventurous</div>
      <div class="tour-info">
        <div class="tour-bar">
          <span class="tour-name">Secret Cenote</span>
          </div>
        <p class="tour-oneline">A cenote not even locals know about. The entrance is an ancient well created by the Maya.</p>
        <span class="tour-toggle">+</span>
      </div>
    </label>
    <div class="tour-body">
      <div class="tour-body-inner">
        <p class="tour-desc">You'll climb down a ladder through the well, down into a private cenote. The family who cares for this land has created a botanical garden from the plants they find on their adventures in the jungle. If this is a private tour, there's an option to skinny dip.</p>
        <div class="tour-meta">
          <span class="meta-pill">4-5 hours</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Underground cenote</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Local Maya family</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Swimming</span>
        </div>
        <img class="tour-addon-photo" src="/images/secret-cenote-addon-local.jpg" alt="The local cenote add-on, with cliff jumping and clear water for snorkeling">
        <p class="tour-desc"><strong>Optional add-on: visit a local cenote with cliff jumping, perfect for free diving and amazing snorkeling. +700 MXN per person.</strong></p>
        <div class="tour-itin">
          <p class="tour-itin-h">Itinerary</p>
          <ul class="tour-itin-list">
            <li>Meet at a cafe in Tulum town</li>
            <li>~20-30 min drive to the cenotes</li>
            <li>Optional add-on: local favorite open cenote (cliff jumping)</li>
            <li>Secret Cave Cenote</li>
            <li>Picnic at the cenote</li>
            <li>Drive back</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-inc">
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Round-trip transport from the cafe</li><li>Professional guide</li><li>Entrance fees</li><li>Life jackets &amp; snorkels</li><li>Snacks</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Not included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Hotel pickup/drop-off (available on request)</li><li>Food beyond snacks</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-foot">
          <span class="tour-price">FROM 2,200 MXN / PERSON</span>
          <a href="#book" class="btn-book">Check Availability →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- INTRO TO CENOTES -->
  <div class="tour">
    <input type="checkbox" id="tour-intro-cenotes">
    <label class="tour-head" for="tour-intro-cenotes">
      <img class="tour-photo" src="/images/secret-cenote-group.jpg" alt="Friends laughing together at an open cenote on the Intro to Cenotes Tour in Tulum">
      <div class="tour-tag">Off the beaten path</div>
      <div class="tour-info">
        <div class="tour-bar">
          <span class="tour-name">Intro to Cenotes Tour</span>
          </div>
        <p class="tour-oneline">Two off-the-beaten-path cenotes, cave and open water.</p>
        <span class="tour-toggle">+</span>
      </div>
    </label>
    <div class="tour-body">
      <div class="tour-body-inner">
        <p class="tour-desc">A tour of two off-the-beaten-path cenotes. Taak Bi Ha is an amazing cave cenote, a cenote in the jungle with great lighting for freediving and stalactite and stalagmite formations. Nicte Ha is a fully open cenote with lily pads, cliff jumping, and amazing snorkeling.</p>
        <div class="tour-meta">
          <span class="meta-pill">4-5 hours</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Cave &amp; open cenote</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Freediving</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Swimming</span>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-itin">
          <p class="tour-itin-h">Itinerary</p>
          <ul class="tour-itin-list">
            <li>Meet at a cafe in Tulum town</li>
            <li>~20-30 min drive to the cenotes</li>
            <li>Taak Bi Ha cave cenote</li>
            <li>Nicte Ha open cenote</li>
            <li>Drive back</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-inc">
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Round-trip transport from the cafe</li><li>Professional guide</li><li>Entrance fees</li><li>Life jackets &amp; snorkels</li><li>Snacks</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Not included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Hotel pickup/drop-off (available on request)</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-foot">
          <span class="tour-price">FROM 2,800 MXN / PERSON</span>
          <a href="#book" class="btn-book">Check Availability →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- MUYIL -->
  <div class="tour">
    <input type="checkbox" id="tour2">
    <label class="tour-head" for="tour2">
      <img class="tour-photo" src="/images/muyil-river-float-group.jpg" alt="Group floating the Muyil River through mangroves and canals">
      <div class="tour-tag">Most relaxing</div>
      <div class="tour-info">
        <div class="tour-bar">
          <span class="tour-name">Muyil River Float</span>
          </div>
        <p class="tour-oneline">The most relaxing day in Tulum, boating through lagoons and mangroves.</p>
        <span class="tour-toggle">+</span>
      </div>
    </label>
    <div class="tour-body">
      <div class="tour-body-inner">
        <p class="tour-desc">Relaxation tour. Float through canals built by the ancient Maya. Boat through lagoons and mangroves. It's the most relaxing day in Tulum, and the one people keep talking about long after they get home. Bring nothing but yourself. The water does the rest.</p>
        <div class="tour-meta">
          <span class="meta-pill">4.5-5.5 hours</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Ancient Mayan canals</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Mangroves &amp; lagoons</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Floating</span>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-itin">
          <p class="tour-itin-h">Itinerary</p>
          <ul class="tour-itin-list">
            <li>Meet at Story Horse Cafe in the morning</li>
            <li>~20-30 min drive to Muyil</li>
            <li>Float the ancient Mayan canals</li>
            <li>Boat through the lagoons and mangroves</li>
            <li>Picnic by the lagoon</li>
            <li>Drive back</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-inc">
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Round-trip transport from the cafe</li><li>Professional guide</li><li>Entrance fees</li><li>Life jackets</li><li>Traditional Mexican &amp; healthy regional snacks</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Not included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Hotel pickup/drop-off (available on request)</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-foot">
          <span class="tour-price">FROM 3,400 MXN / PERSON</span>
          <a href="#book" class="btn-book">Check Availability →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- STORIES BEHIND THE STOREFRONT -->
  <div class="tour">
    <input type="checkbox" id="tour3">
    <label class="tour-head" for="tour3">
      <img class="tour-photo" src="/images/la-guarida-workshop-group.jpg" alt="A group workshop at La Guarida, a local cultural center in Tulum, on the Town Chisme tour">
      <div class="tour-tag">Culture &amp; food</div>
      <div class="tour-info">
        <div class="tour-bar">
          <span class="tour-name">Town Chisme</span>
          </div>
        <p class="tour-oneline">Explore the local side of Tulum.</p>
        <span class="tour-toggle">+</span>
      </div>
    </label>
    <div class="tour-body">
      <div class="tour-body-inner">
        <p class="tour-desc">Find out what it's like to live in Tulum. Get the chisme, eat our favorite food, and go out to the places that make people want to call this place home. This is the town behind the town, the locally-owned shops, the makers, and the people whose stories you'd never hear as a tourist passing through. We stop where the owners know us by name, explore vintage and thrift stores, taste what the neighborhood actually eats, and trade the polished tourist version of Tulum for the real one. You'll leave knowing the difference between the Tulum people visit and the Tulum people live in.</p>
        <div class="tour-meta">
          <span class="meta-pill">3-4 hours</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Local shops &amp; makers</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Vintage &amp; thrift</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Coffee &amp; breakfast included</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Walking</span>
        </div>
        <img class="tour-addon-photo" src="/images/IMG_2627.jpeg" alt="Exploring a mural on the Town Chisme, stories behind the storefront, tour in Tulum" style="aspect-ratio:3/4;object-position:center 25%;">
        <div class="tour-itin">
          <p class="tour-itin-h">Sample Itinerary</p>
          <ul class="tour-itin-list">
            <li>Meet in Tulum town center</li>
            <li>Share a meal together at a local restaurant</li>
            <li>Explore murals around town</li>
            <li>Learn local chisme (for example, Tulum as a municipality is only 17 years old)</li>
            <li>Learn the nuances of Tulum's different neighborhoods (La Veleta, Cancha Maya, Centro, Aldea Zama, Tumben Ka'a)</li>
            <li>Visit Ladle, a local community center, for snacks and more</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);font-style:italic;margin-top:6px;">Personalized based on what your group wants to see and do. This is just a taste of what's included.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-inc">
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Professional guide</li><li>Food and drink at the local stops</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Not included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Clothes/items you buy while shopping</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-foot">
          <span class="tour-price">FROM 2,500 MXN / PERSON</span>
          <a href="#book" class="btn-book">Check Availability →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- STREET FOOD -->
  <div class="tour">
    <input type="checkbox" id="tour4">
    <label class="tour-head" for="tour4">
      <img class="tour-photo" src="/images/food-tour-sitdown.jpg" alt="A friend celebrating over bao buns at a Tulum restaurant on the Food Tour" style="object-position:center 20%;">
      <div class="tour-tag">Food · Drinks included</div>
      <div class="tour-info">
        <div class="tour-bar">
          <span class="tour-name">Food Tour</span>
          </div>
        <p class="tour-oneline">Explore prehispanic Mexican food and the amazing fusions that make Tulum one of the best places to eat.</p>
        <span class="tour-toggle">+</span>
      </div>
    </label>
    <div class="tour-body">
      <div class="tour-body-inner">
        <p class="tour-desc">Explore prehispanic Mexican food and the amazing fusions that make Tulum one of the best places to eat. Choose your style: three of our favorite street food stops, or three sit-down spots. Street food or sit-down, your choice.</p>
        <div class="tour-meta">
          <span class="meta-pill">3-4 hours</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Food &amp; drinks included</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Street food or sit-down</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Local spots</span>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-itin">
          <p class="tour-itin-h">Itinerary</p>
          <ul class="tour-itin-list">
            <li>Meet in Tulum town</li>
            <li>Choose your style: three street food stops, or three sit-down spots</li>
            <li>Transportation between stops, walking or driving depending on the day</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-inc">
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Food &amp; drinks</li><li>Local guide</li><li>Transportation between stops</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Not included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Hotel pickup/drop-off</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-foot">
          <span class="tour-price">PRICE BY EXPERIENCE</span>
          <a href="#book" class="btn-book">Check Availability →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- MONKEY SPOTTING -->
  <div class="tour">
    <input type="checkbox" id="tour5">
    <label class="tour-head" for="tour5">
      <img class="tour-photo" src="/images/monkey-spotting-lagoon.jpg" alt="Looking out over the lagoon at Punta Laguna on the Monkey Spotting tour">
      <div class="tour-tag">Full day adventure</div>
      <div class="tour-info">
        <div class="tour-bar">
          <span class="tour-name">Monkey Spotting + Lagoon Jungle Adventure</span>
          </div>
        <p class="tour-oneline">Our most adventurous tour. Spend the day in the jungle looking for wild monkeys.</p>
        <span class="tour-toggle">+</span>
      </div>
    </label>
    <div class="tour-body">
      <div class="tour-body-inner">
        <p class="tour-desc">Our most adventurous tour. Spend the day in the jungle looking for wild monkeys while enjoying swimming, canoeing, and zip lining over a pristine lagoon. And because your guide is a UCLA wildlife biologist, you'll actually understand what you're looking at, not just see it. Includes picnic lunch.</p>
        <div class="tour-meta">
          <span class="meta-pill">Full day</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Wild spider monkeys</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Zip line &amp; canoe</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Lunch included</span>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-itin">
          <p class="tour-itin-h">Itinerary</p>
          <ul class="tour-itin-list">
            <li>Meet in Tulum town</li>
            <li>~1.5 hour drive to the lagoon</li>
            <li>A moment of intention with a local guide before entering the jungle</li>
            <li>Walk the jungle looking for wild spider monkeys</li>
            <li>Harness up and rappel into a cenote holding an underwater ancient Maya burial site</li>
            <li>Zip line</li>
            <li>Canoe</li>
            <li>Play in the lagoon, a full picnic spread on the dock, shaded area to relax</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);font-style:italic;margin-top:6px;">Order can vary by day.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-inc">
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>UCLA wildlife biologist guide</li><li>Zip line &amp; canoe</li><li>Picnic lunch</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="tour-inc-h">Not included</p>
            <ul class="tour-inc-list"><li>Hotel pickup/drop-off</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-foot">
          <span class="tour-price">FROM 4,000 MXN / PERSON</span>
          <a href="#book" class="btn-book">Check Availability →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  </div>

  <div class="tours-note">
    <strong>Honeymooners, couples, friend groups, solo travelers, all welcome.</strong> Every tour is small. Bigger group, retreat, or event? That becomes a private tour, sized and priced for your group.
  </div>

  <div class="tours-note">
    <strong>Want something more low-key?</strong> The Food Tour and Town Chisme are easy, walkable days if cenotes and jungle hikes aren't your thing.
  </div>

  <div class="tours-gallery">
    <img src="/images/secret-cenote-cave.jpg" alt="Entering the Secret Cenote through the cave">
    <img src="/images/muyil-river-float-group.jpg" alt="Group on the Muyil River Float tour">
    <img src="/images/punta-laguna-canoes.jpg" alt="Canoes at Punta Laguna">
    <img src="/images/tours-gallery-boat.jpg" alt="Boating through the mangroves">
    <img src="/images/tours-gallery-picnic.jpg" alt="Picnic with local fruit on tour">
    <img src="/images/food-tour-street-snack.jpg" alt="A street snack on the Food Tour in Tulum">
    <img src="/images/food-tour-sitdown.jpg" alt="A sit-down restaurant experience on the Food Tour in Tulum">
  </div>

</section>

<section class="reviews" id="tour-reviews">
  <p class="sec-eye" style="color:var(--white);">Don't take our word for it</p>
  <h2>What people say</h2>
  <p class="scroll-hint">← swipe to read more →</p>
  <div class="review-scroll">
    <div class="rcard">
      <div class="rstars">★★★★★</div>
      <input type="checkbox" id="trev1" class="rev-toggle">
      <p class="rtext">Ay ay ay, what a time!!! Santi was a dream. The entire tour, start to finish, through Tulum and into the jungle and down into the cenote was better than I ever could've imagined.</p>
      <label for="trev1" class="rev-more">Read more</label>
      <p class="rname">— Corinna Harris, Google review</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rcard">
      <div class="rstars">★★★★★</div>
      <input type="checkbox" id="trev2" class="rev-toggle">
      <p class="rtext">My partner and I booked two tours with Santi during our trip to Tulum, Street Food in the evening and Cenotes the next day. Before the trip, Santi was incredibly communicative and helpful as I planned, offering amazing local recs.</p>
      <label for="trev2" class="rev-more">Read more</label>
      <p class="rname">— Madge Dietrich, Google review</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rcard">
      <div class="rstars">★★★★★</div>
      <input type="checkbox" id="trev3" class="rev-toggle">
      <p class="rtext">We found Santi on Reddit while looking for queer experiences in Tulum and had a great tailored tour of the Muyil river. During the tour, they use their extensive knowledge in marine biology to share facts about the river.</p>
      <label for="trev3" class="rev-more">Read more</label>
      <p class="rname">— Diana Ledesma, Google review</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/place/Queerness+Experiences/@20.4203707,-87.5893973,94594m/data=!3m1!1e3!4m8!3m7!1s0x213eac5d05676035:0x9ad4bb88e0a769c2!8m2!3d20.4200372!4d-87.259726!9m1!1b1!16s%2Fg%2F11w4tpph1c?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-reviews">Read all reviews on Google →</a>
</section>

<section class="faq" id="tour-faq">
  <p class="sec-eye">Before you book</p>
  <h2>Reservations &amp;<br>cancellations</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <div class="faq-item">
      <input type="checkbox" id="tfaq1" checked>
      <label class="faq-q" for="tfaq1">How do I reserve a tour?<span class="tog">+</span></label>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Fill out the form below with your dates and the tour you want, and I'll check availability. Once we've confirmed a date, your spot is reserved with a 50% deposit via Zelle, Wise, or PayPal (5% fee applies to PayPal).</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <input type="checkbox" id="tfaq2">
      <label class="faq-q" for="tfaq2">What's the cancellation policy?<span class="tog">+</span></label>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Full refund if you cancel a week or more before your tour. 50% refund if you cancel between 48 hours and 6 days out. Inside 48 hours, deposits are non-refundable. Tours happen rain or shine.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta" id="book">
  <p class="cta-eye">Check availability</p>
  <h2>When are you<br>arriving?</h2>
  <p>Tell me your dates and which tour caught your eye. I'll check availability and follow up with everything you need to lock it in.</p>
  <form class="cta-form" name="contact" method="POST" data-netlify="true" action="/thank-you">
    <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="contact" />
    <div class="cta-row2">
      <input class="cta-in" type="text" name="first_name" placeholder="First name" required>
      <input class="cta-in" type="text" name="last_name" placeholder="Last name">
    </div>
    <input class="cta-in" type="text" name="pronouns" placeholder="Pronouns (e.g. she/her, they/them)">
    <input class="cta-in" type="email" name="email" placeholder="Email" required>
    <input class="cta-in" type="tel" name="whatsapp" placeholder="WhatsApp (include country code, e.g. +1 555 123 4567)">
    <input class="cta-in" type="text" name="dates" placeholder="Dates you're coming to Tulum">
    <input class="cta-in" type="text" name="group-size" placeholder="How many people in your group?">
    <select class="cta-in cta-select" name="tour">
      <option value="" disabled selected>Which tour interests you?</option>
      <option>Secret Cenote</option>
      <option>Intro to Cenotes Tour</option>
      <option>Muyil River Float</option>
      <option>Secret Cenote + Muyil (both)</option>
      <option>Town Chisme</option>
      <option>Food Tour</option>
      <option>Monkey Spotting + Lagoon Jungle Adventure</option>
      <option>Group trip or retreat</option>
      <option>Not sure yet, help me choose</option>
    </select>
    <textarea class="cta-in" name="message" rows="3" placeholder="What's up? Tell me what you're looking for"></textarea>
    <button type="submit" class="btn-cta-form">Send. I'll reply within 24 hours</button>
  </form>
</section>

</Layout>

<style is:global>
@font-face{font-family:'CheddarGothicStencil';src:url('/fonts/CheddarGothicStencil.woff2') format('woff2');font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;font-display:swap;}
*,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0;}
html{overflow-x:hidden;max-width:100vw;}
:root{
  --magenta:#C8185A;--yellow:#F5A623;--terra:#B5390F;--dark:#1a1a18;
  --white:#FDFCF9;--bone:#F5F0E8;--muted:#4A4034;--border:rgba(26,26,24,0.12);
  --s-sm:16px;--s-md:32px;--s-lg:64px;
  --ff:'Archivo Black','Space Grotesk',sans-serif;--fb:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;
}
